From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: data object formats, folder custom settings, SHLimitInputEdit (2049)

shell32: data object formats, SHGetSetFolderCustomSettings, SHLimitInputEdit.

The shell's data object offers the file formats (HDROP, FileName, FileNameW)
only for items that are files; an item that is not (My Computer, Control
Panel) has the item list and the preferred drop effect, link. Its format
enumerator's Skip leaves the position at the end when it skips too far, and a
copy starts over. SHGetItemFromDataObject keeps its error when there is no
file list. SHGetSetFolderCustomSettings reads desktop.ini (icon, info tip,
logo, class id) and writes the same; SHLimitInputEdit keeps the characters a
file name cannot have out of an edit control, typed or pasted. They were
stubs or fell short.
---
